Subject: [PATCH 51/69] fix(ui): add exponential backoff with jitter to
 WebSocket reconnection (#156)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* fix(ui): add exponential backoff with jitter to WebSocket reconnection

Replace fixed 3-second retry interval with exponential backoff (3s → 60s max)
and ±20% jitter to prevent thundering herd. Reset backoff on successful
connection and when user returns to the page (visibility change).

Closes #155

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* refactor(ui): extract duplicated reconnect scheduling into helper closure

Consolidate the identical backoff-increment + spawn-delayed-reconnect
logic from ConnectionLost and Connect::Err into a single
schedule_reconnect closure, reducing duplication.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix: address review feedback — correct first-retry delay and cap jitter

- Compute delay before incrementing failure count so first retry is 3s (not 6s)
- Cap jitter result to RECONNECT_MAX_MS so delay never exceeds 60s
- Add u32::MAX edge case test

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

